# 1. DISTINCT

## Simple Definition

DISTINCT is used to remove duplicate values from the result.

## Why it is Used

- Find unique values
- Remove repeated records
- Generate summarized reports

## Syntax

```sql
SELECT DISTINCT column_name
FROM table_name;
```

## Examples

```sql
SELECT DISTINCT Country
FROM Netflix_Content;
```

```sql
SELECT DISTINCT Genre
FROM Netflix_Content;
```

```sql
SELECT DISTINCT Type
FROM Netflix_Content;
```

```sql
SELECT DISTINCT Country, Genre
FROM Netflix_Content;
```

## Important Points

- Removes duplicate values.
- Returns only unique records.
- Works on one or multiple columns.

## Common Mistake

```sql
SELECT Country DISTINCT
FROM Netflix_Content;
```

## Short Summary

DISTINCT returns unique values from a column.

---

# 2. ALIAS

## Simple Definition

ALIAS gives a temporary name to a column.

## Why it is Used

- Improve readability
- Display meaningful column names
- Create user-friendly reports

## Syntax

```sql
SELECT column_name AS alias_name
FROM table_name;
```

## Examples

```sql
SELECT Title AS Show_Name
FROM Netflix_Content;
```

```sql
SELECT Release_Year AS Year_Released
FROM Netflix_Content;
```

```sql
SELECT Duration_Min AS Duration
FROM Netflix_Content;
```

```sql
SELECT Genre AS Category
FROM Netflix_Content;
```

### Alias with Calculated Columns

```sql
SELECT Title,
       Duration_Min / 60.0 AS Duration_Hours
FROM Netflix_Content;
```

## Important Points

- Alias exists only in query output.
- AS keyword is optional.
- Alias can be used with calculations.

## Common Mistake

```sql
SELECT AS Show_Name Title
FROM Netflix_Content;
```

## Short Summary

Alias provides a temporary name to a column.

