# 6. ORDER BY

## Simple Definition

ORDER BY sorts records.

## Why it is Used

- Display data neatly
- Sort reports
- Find latest or oldest content

## Syntax

```sql
SELECT *
FROM table_name
ORDER BY column_name;
```

## Examples

```sql
SELECT *
FROM Netflix_Content
ORDER BY Release_Year;
```

```sql
SELECT *
FROM Netflix_Content
ORDER BY Release_Year DESC;
```

```sql
SELECT *
FROM Netflix_Content
ORDER BY Title;
```

```sql
SELECT *
FROM Netflix_Content
ORDER BY Duration_Min DESC;
```

## Multiple Column Sorting

```sql
SELECT *
FROM Netflix_Content
ORDER BY Genre,
         Release_Year DESC;
```

### Explanation

- First sort by Genre
- Then sort Release_Year in descending order within each Genre

## Important Points

- ASC = Ascending (default)
- DESC = Descending
- Can sort multiple columns

## Common Mistake

```sql
ORDER Release_Year BY
```

## Short Summary

ORDER BY sorts records in ascending or descending order.

